(Fixture for tests/270: what a generated program looks like at the
 moment one of the ledger's leaf assertions fails - a few ordinary lines
 of output, then the one ASSERT line the failing check prints, then exit
 95. Planted by hand, because the generator can only produce this when
 the compiler is actually wrong about a documented result, which is the
 thing the whole channel exists to catch and cannot be arranged on
 demand.

 The second ASSERT line is deliberate: only the LAST one is followed by
 the exit, so it is the one that killed the program and the only one
 worth carrying as the finding's detail.)
Print "the inbox size 11".
Print "ASSERT BUF-12: expected 1 got 1 (this one held and kept going)".
Print "the inbox capacity 64".
If 1 is equal to 1 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-05: expected 4097 got 4096", Exit 95. Print "unreachable".
Print "unreachable".
